The generated GFN2-D4 reference data in d4_data.hpp is derived from dftd4:

  https://github.com/dftd4/dftd4
  revision 6e1f59c3f39d919a2dbef0601d2576727c8b30e8
  SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-3.0-or-later

The underlying charge-dependent D4 model is described in:

  E. Caldeweyher et al., J. Chem. Phys. 150, 154122 (2019)
  https://doi.org/10.1063/1.5090222

The D4-specific electronegativity-weighted coordination-number implementation
also follows mctc-lib revision e9de066d89f250d1cfb6de3a33f0c27c0e2f855d,
which is licensed under Apache-2.0.

The corresponding license texts are redistributed beside this notice in
data/parameters/licenses. xtbloom keeps the exact source revisions and a digest
of every parsed source blob in d4_manifest.json.

VibeQC stores the symmetric reference C6 matrix as a lossless lower triangle.
GFN2 reference charges and polarizabilities are not generic EEQ reference data.

The generated EEQ-D4 data in d4_eeq_data.hpp additionally derives from:

  multicharge revision 6a5d63f9e9e29dcf13cc47cc27f33bf9015681bf
  SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

and mctc-lib revision e9de066d89f250d1cfb6de3a33f0c27c0e2f855d
for the EEQ2019 coordination-number convention and covalent radii
(SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0). The DFT-D4 EEQ reference charges,
reference polarizabilities and C6 data retain the upstream DFT-D4
LGPL-3.0-or-later provenance. Exact source blobs and hashes are recorded in
d4_eeq_manifest.json.

Standard EEQ-D4 and r2SCAN-3c do not share one C6 table: the latter changes
the charge-scaling parameters from ga/gc=3/2 to 2/1. Both pinned profiles are
therefore generated and identified separately; no runtime dftd4 or
multicharge dependency is introduced.
